283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 182 0 R
/T (In contemporary psychological discourse, the inner critic is broadly defined as the internalized voice or set of voices that disparage, berate, and undermine our sense of self-worth and competence. This critical inner dialogue is shaped by a myriad of factors, including early childhood experiences, societal influences, and cultural norms. It operates on a subconscious level, frequently evading our conscious awareness yet exerting a profound impact on our thoughts, emotions, and behaviors.)
/E (In contemporary psychological discourse, the inner critic is broadly defined as the internalized voice or set of voices that disparage, berate, and undermine our sense of self-worth and competence. This critical inner dialogue is shaped by a myriad of factors, including early childhood experiences, societal influences, and cultural norms. It operates on a subconscious level, frequently evading our conscious awareness yet exerting a profound impact on our thoughts, emotions, and behaviors.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
