/T (Attachment theory, proposed by John Bowlby in the mid-20th century, offers a profound lens through which to understand the dynamics of human relationships and emotional development. At its core, attachment theory posits that our early experiences with caregivers profoundly shape our patterns of relating to others and ourselves throughout life. In this chapter, we will explore the basics of attachment theory and examine its relevance to the concept of the inner critic.)
/E (Attachment theory, proposed by John Bowlby in the mid-20th century, offers a profound lens through which to understand the dynamics of human relationships and emotional development. At its core, attachment theory posits that our early experiences with caregivers profoundly shape our patterns of relating to others and ourselves throughout life. In this chapter, we will explore the basics of attachment theory and examine its relevance to the concept of the inner critic.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
