/Title (Experiential strategies in Schema Therapy offer powerful tools to reduce or silence the inner critic. By engaging deeply with emotions and memories through techniques like imagery rescripting, chair work, limited reparenting, and schema mode imagery, individuals can transform their inner dialogue and foster self-compassion. These strategies empower individuals to reclaim their self-worth and build a more supportive, nurturing inner voice, paving the way for lasting emotional healing and growth.)
