/Title (In contemporary psychological discourse, the inner critic is broadly defined as the internalized voice or set of voices that disparage, berate, and undermine our sense of self-worth and competence. This critical inner dialogue is shaped by a myriad of factors, including early childhood experiences, societal influences, and cultural norms. It operates on a subconscious level, frequently evading our conscious awareness yet exerting a profound impact on our thoughts, emotions, and behaviors.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2396 0 R
>>
endobj
