/Title (Conversely, when caregivers are unavailable, inconsistent, or abusive, we may internalize beliefs about ourselves as unworthy, unlovable, or inadequate. These negative internal working models serve as fertile ground for the emergence of the inner critic, which perpetuates and reinforces these maladaptive beliefs through relentless self-criticism and judgment.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2413 0 R
/Prev 2418 0 R
